From: Jihyeon Gim <potatogim@gluesys.com>
Subject: [PATCH] screencast: tie in-flight frame lifetime to its buffer

Backport upstream 5724a432fc95690aef19e55e62178d71b60d0cbb
("screencast: tie frame lifetime to the buffer") to fixed 0.8.1.
Only hunk offsets/context differ: 0.8.1 lacks the later remove-buffer
diagnostic. Keep the actual ext and wlr frame cancellation, PAUSED cleanup,
and buffer-removal behavior; retain the original authorization session.

The upstream author identifies frames left attached to removed storage
and a second create_frame while the earlier frame is still alive. This
is a producer fix for the CI-owned validation desktop, not an application
workaround or a claim about the user's separately installed Portal.

Upstream: https://github.com/emersion/xdg-desktop-portal-wlr/commit/5724a432fc95690aef19e55e62178d71b60d0cbb
Base: e1d5d16f0e064a0b788c5d70c11461b15ee7a4af (0.8.1)
License: MIT; Copyright (c) 2018 emersion. Preserve upstream LICENSE.
Backport preparation: huhucapture maintainers

